1. **An organic electroluminescence device comprising:**

a substrate;

a plurality of unit regions disposed on the substrate and spatially separated from one another, each unit region being partitioned into a light-emitting area and a non-emissive area;

an organic light-emitting diode element disposed in the light-emitting area of each unit region, the organic light-emitting diode element comprising a first electrode, an organic electroluminescent layer, and a second electrode; and

a light absorption layer disposed in the non-emissive area of each unit region and configured to absorb incident light,

wherein the organic light-emitting diode element is configured to emit light from the light-emitting area, and the light absorption layer is laterally separated from the organic electroluminescent layer within the respective unit region.
